      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors present a series of 98 aorta-coronary bypass procedures without the help of Extracorporeal Circulation. Indications and technique are detailed. There was no hospital mortality and short-term results are satisfactory. This technique, feasible in about 10% of all cases, should be considered especially in old patients, in case of chronic renal insufficiency and in redo surgery."},
